  "rdfs:range": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float",
  "status": "stable",
  "added": "2026-04-19",
  "notes": "0 means the position is essentially a guess; 100 is exact. Useful when the Place comes from GPS, IP geolocation, or any source whose precision varies. Distinct from `as:radius` (the size of the area covered) — accuracy describes the *uncertainty* of the centre point.",
  "examples": [
